DFlash2 drafter, v0.29.0 base: the W4A16 KV-dequant slice.

The old form of this bundle (written against 0.27.1) vendored the ENTIRE DFlash2
drafter: the DFlash2DraftModel (grouped dynamic convolution + candidate selector,
vLLM PR #52816 by SubSir), its V2-runner speculator, the is_causal precedence, and
the K-slot / V2-forcing / registry / dispatch wiring, plus the DFlash prepare-inputs
and rejection-sampler hardening. As of the v0.29.0 base ALL of that is stock: the
model (model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash2.py) and the speculator
(v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash2/) ship in the image, the dispatch in
v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/__init__.py already routes DFlash2DraftModel ->
DFlash2Speculator, and the base qwen3_dflash.py already carries
decoder_layer_cls / model_cls plus the is_causal precedence. Re-applying any of
that is a no-op or a red hunk, so none of it is in this patch anymore.

What this slice adds on top of stock 0.29.0, and why it is kept:
  * _dense_kv_rows (new module-level function in qwen3_dflash.py). The drafter's
    context-KV precompute reads the [q_size:] rows of each layer's qkv_proj. Stock
    slices a plain 2-D weight; a compressed-tensors W4A16/W8A16 qkv_proj stores
    pack-quantized weights, so this dequantizes them (weight_packed * weight_scale)
    back to a dense bf16 matrix at load time, before the Marlin repack.
  * _build_context_kv_buffers: re-point the one kv_weights list-comprehension to
    that helper, so a quantized drafter's context KV precomputes correctly.

That is what lets the box's DFlash2 drafter be W4A16 (small enough to sit beside
the W4A8 27B at 262K / 0.90) while still precomputing its KV. The drafter's lm_head
is the target's, and 0.29.0's LogitsProcessor._apply_head already routes any
quantized head through quant_method.apply(), so no head patch is needed here either.

Dropped (speed only, not load-bearing on this box): the small-k top-k (k_max)
sampler path and the selector's top-k/top-p proposal truncation that the old bundle
carried. The conv+selector acceptance gain — the actual reason DFlash2 beats the
built-in MTP drafter — is entirely stock in 0.29.0.

Provenance: the W4A16 drafter and this dequant derive from the syv-ai
qwen38-27b-rtx3090 DFlash2 work (see README). Attribution is kept in the README;
this header only carries what the patch does.

Apply from the installed vllm package dir, after the other patches:
  patch -p1 -d <site-packages>/vllm < dflash2-backport.patch
One file, two hunks. It re-anchors cleanly on the v0.29.0 base only; on any other
base the kv_weights anchor line moves and the apply is a red "find another base"
signal, not a hunk to hand-nudge.

--- a/model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash.py
+++ b/model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash.py
@@ -355,6 +355,27 @@
         return hidden_states, residual
 
 
+
+def _dense_kv_rows(attn: nn.Module) -> torch.Tensor:
+    """Rows [q_size:] of the qkv projection as a dense bf16 matrix. For a compressed-tensors
+    W4A16/W8A16 (pack-quantized, symmetric, group) qkv_proj this is called from load_weights,
+    i.e. before the Marlin repack, so weight_packed/weight_scale are still in the plain
+    checkpoint layout and can be dequantized here."""
+    qkv = attn.qkv_proj
+    w = getattr(qkv, "weight", None)
+    if w is not None and w.dim() == 2:
+        return w[attn.q_size :]
+    packed, scale = qkv.weight_packed, qkv.weight_scale
+    # (weight_shape holds only the last-loaded shard of a fused qkv; use the tensors.)
+    out_f, in_f = int(packed.shape[0]), int(qkv.input_size)
+    bits = 32 * packed.shape[1] // in_f
+    from compressed_tensors.compressors.pack_quantized.base import unpack_from_int32
+    q = unpack_from_int32(packed.data, bits, torch.Size([out_f, in_f]), packed_dim=1)
+    group = in_f // scale.shape[1]
+    dense = (q.to(torch.float32).reshape(out_f, in_f // group, group)
+             * scale.to(torch.float32)[..., None]).reshape(out_f, in_f)
+    return dense.to(scale.dtype if scale.dtype.is_floating_point else torch.bfloat16)[attn.q_size :]
+
 @support_torch_compile
 class DFlashQwen3Model(nn.Module):
     decoder_layer_cls = DFlashQwen3DecoderLayer
@@ -469,7 +490,7 @@
         self._hidden_norm_weight = self.hidden_norm.weight.data
 
         # KV projection weights: [num_layers * 2 * kv_size, hidden_size]
-        kv_weights = [a.qkv_proj.weight[a.q_size :] for a in layers_attn]
+        kv_weights = [_dense_kv_rows(a) for a in layers_attn]
         self._fused_kv_weight = torch.cat(kv_weights, dim=0)
         if has_bias:
             kv_biases = [a.qkv_proj.bias[a.q_size :] for a in layers_attn]
